 all 8 year-on-year comparisons, so this is a trend rather than one good quarter.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1841156/000119312526204469/0001193125-26-204469-index.htm","accession":"0001193125-26-204469"},{"text":"Operating cash flow is positive at $96.6m over the trailing year, so the business funds itself and is not dependent on raising money.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1841156/000119312526204469/0001193125-26-204469-index.htm","accession":"0001193125-26-204469"},{"text":"Net cash of $338.8m against total assets of $698.6m - no debt overhang forcing decisions.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1841156/000119312526204469/0001193125-26-204469-index.htm","accession":"0001193125-26-204469"},{"text":"Share count is close to flat (0.4% over the year), so growth in the business accrues to existing holders rather than being diluted away.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1841156/000119312526204469/0001193125-26-204469-index.htm","accession":"0001193125-26-204469"}],"bear":[{"text":"Gross margin is only 24.1%, so scale has to be enormous before anything reaches the bottom line.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1841156/000119312526204469/0001193125-26-204469-index.htm","accession":"0001193125-26-204469"},{"text":"Base rate: 57.8% of US common stocks underperformed one-month Treasury bills over their lifetimes (Bessembinder, Journal of Financial Economics, 2018). Nothing above changes that starting point.","source_url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jfineco.2018.06.004"}],"triggers":[{"id":"gross_margin_floor","kind":"metric","label":"Gross margin falls below 16.0% for 2 consecutive quarters","metric":"gross_margin","comparison":"below","threshold":0.16,"consecutive":2,"current":0.241,"current_display":"24.1%","threshold_display":"16.0%","fired":false,"rationale":"Eight points of margin is a real deterioration rather than noise. Two consecutive quarters stops on